.TH DC 1 "DeviceCryptor" "Vassbrekke AS" "User commands"
.SH NAME
dc \- DeviceCryptor encrypted containers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dc
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dc
creates and mounts experimental encrypted file containers.
The native format is DC01 (AES-256-XTS, Argon2id, BLAKE3 header MAC).
Some VeraCrypt/TrueCrypt volumes can be mounted on the AES-XTS path.
This is not a VeraCrypt replacement and is not independently audited.
Do not store irreplaceable data in these volumes.
.PP
Omit
.B --password
to type it silently. Prefer
.B --password-env
over
.B --password
so the secret is not visible in the process list.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B create
.I path
.RB [ --size
.IR SIZE ]
.RB [ --fs
fat32|ext4|none]
.RB [ --wipe ]
Create a DC01 container.
.I SIZE
accepts bytes or a human suffix:
.BR 16M ,
.BR 1G ,
.BR 512K .
.B --wipe
fills the file with random data and prints a progress meter on stderr.
.TP
.B mount
.I path
.I mountpoint
Mount a volume. On Linux, FAT volumes use an unprivileged checkout by default.
.B --live
mounts FAT through FUSE so edits write through. That command stays running.
Dismount does not ask for the password again.
.RB [ --prf
auto|sha512|sha256|blake2s|whirlpool|streebog|argon2]
selects the VeraCrypt PKCS-5 PRF. auto tries Argon2id, then HMAC-SHA-512, HMAC-SHA-256, HMAC-BLAKE2s, HMAC-Whirlpool, and HMAC-Streebog.
.TP
.B dismount
.RB [ --id
.IR ID ]
Sync changes back and forget the mount session.
.TP
.B chpasswd
.I path
Change a DC01 password without re-encrypting volume data.
.TP
.B header backup
.I container
.I outfile
.TP
.B header restore
.I container
.I infile
.TP
.B status
List active mounts.
.TP
.B info
.I path
Show unlocked volume metadata, including the disk cipher.
.TP
.B bench
.RB [ --pim
.IR N ]
Time DC01 Argon2id defaults. With
.BR --pim ,
also time VeraCrypt's Argon2id mapping (0 means default PIM 12 and can be slow).
.TP
.B keyfile
.I path
.RB [ --bytes
.IR N ]
Write a random keyfile, mode 0600. Default length is 64 bytes.
.TP
.B favorite
list | add | remove
.TP
.B keywrap
gen | wrap | unwrap
ML-KEM-768 key-export wrap. Not a disk cipher.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/devicecryptor/
Mount metadata. The unlocked master key is stored in the user kernel keyring when
.B keyctl
can round-trip it; otherwise it is a mode-0600 session file, wiped on dismount.
.SH SEE ALSO
.B devicecryptor
(graphical window, classic layout)
.SH CAVEATS
Experimental. Not independently audited. Twofish, Camellia, AES-Twofish, Kuznyechik-Twofish, Kuznyechik-AES, and Camellia-Kuznyechik are implemented. Serpent and Serpent cascades are not.
System encryption is not ready.
